---
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="section migration-section reveal">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Migration</p>
      <h2>From your current server.</h2>
      <p>
        There are two real paths in, depending on what you have access to.
        Neither one asks you to rewrite your cookbooks before you start.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="migration-paths">
      <article class="path-card">
        <p class="path-kicker">Path 01 · You have a backup</p>
        <h3>Import a knife ec backup.</h3>
        <p>
          <code>import-knife-backup</code> reads the repository written by
          <code>knife ec backup</code> directly. It preserves users, password
          hashes when the key dump contains them, organizations, clients, ACLs,
          cookbooks, and local cookbook blobs.
        </p>
        <p>
          A knife backup does not contain cookbook artifacts, policies, OAuth
          applications, search indexes, or <code>kvpair</code> secrets. Those
          are reconciled separately.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="path-card">
        <p class="path-kicker">Path 02 · You have the live server</p>
        <h3>Crawl the legacy API.</h3>
        <p>
          <code>from-api</code> reads the running server through its API:
          organizations, users, clients, groups, nodes, roles, environments,
          data bags, cookbooks, policies, and ACLs.
        </p>
        <p>
          The legacy API cannot copy password hashes or the admin flag, so those
          users need a password reset or an external identity after the move.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="migration-repoint">
      <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Repoint clients and DNS at your pace.</h3>
        <p>
          The API surface is the same. Move a few nodes, watch a converge, then
          move the rest when you are ready.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="compat-note">
      Snapshot export and import move a Microwave store between SQLite and
      PostgreSQL; they are not the stock-server import path.
      <a href={site.docs}>Migration documentation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
